+# Migrating to v2
+
+The v2 module is a new major version. Change imports from `example.com/portnum`
+to `example.com/portnum/v2`, then handle the new error result:
+
+```go
+port, err := portnum.Parse(text)
+if err != nil {
+	// Reject or report the invalid setting.
+	return err
+}
+usePort(port)
+```
+
+`Parse` accepts only one or more ASCII decimal digits representing 0 through
+65535. Leading zeros remain valid. Empty strings, signs, whitespace, other
+characters, and out-of-range values now return zero and an error; v1 silently
+returned zero for all invalid input, making it indistinguishable from port 0.
+The v1 module remains available at its original import path.
